From: ppptran <ppptran@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: yt921x: keep AN_LINK_EN armed on carrier loss

The port MAC latches the link of an integral PHY on the rising edge of
AN_LINK_EN. Clearing the admin mask on every link-down disarms it, so a
PHY renegotiation (cable replug, re-autonegotiation) drops the link while
the port is disarmed and the subsequent link-up edge is never latched.
PORT_STATUS keeps reporting no link and the port stays dead until the
netdev is administratively cycled, because only the down/up path arms the
port before the PHY link returns.

Keep AN_LINK_EN set for internal ports when the link drops and gate the
data path through the RX/TX enables only. External ports still go through
the full serdes down sequence.

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x_port.c
@@ -959,7 +959,19 @@
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&priv->ports[port].mib_read);
 
 	mutex_lock(&priv->reg_lock);
-	res = yt921x_port_down(priv, port);
+	if (yt921x_is_external_port(priv, port)) {
+		res = yt921x_port_down(priv, port);
+	} else {
+		/* The port latches its integral PHY link on the rising edge of
+		 * AN_LINK_EN. Keep it armed across carrier loss, otherwise the
+		 * latch misses the link returning after a PHY renegotiation
+		 * and the port stays dead until an administrative down/up.
+		 * The data path is still gated by the RX/TX enables.
+		 */
+		res = yt921x_reg_clear_bits(priv, YT921X_PORTn_CTRL(port),
+					    YT921X_PORT_RX_MAC_EN |
+					    YT921X_PORT_TX_MAC_EN);
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&priv->reg_lock);
 
 	if (res)
